        "original_id": "f44d5af1-934e-52bf-aaea-c453b081c19a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Jane Phillips-Matz, Giuseppe Verdi\n- Organizations: Columbia University, Smith College\n- Places: Lebanon, Ohio; Italy; United States; Busseto; Upper Manhattan; New York City\n- Topics: education, biography, academic research, universities\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754.\n- Columbia University is officially named Columbia University in the City of New York.\n- Columbia University is a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz was born in Lebanon, Ohio.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz was educated at Smith College and Columbia University.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz lived for many years in Italy.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz returned to the United States in the early 1970s.\n- After returning to the United States, Mary Jane Phillips-Matz spent her summers in Busseto, Giuseppe Verdi's hometown, where she continued exhaustive research into his life.",
